          "content": "equivalent to $p \\vee q$",
          "is_correct": false
        }
      ],
      "solution": "Let $P = p \\wedge \\sim q$ and $Q = p \\to \\sim q \\equiv \\sim p \\vee \\sim q$.\nWe want to find truth value of $P \\to Q$.\nIf $P$ is True $\\implies p$ is T and $q$ is F.\nThen $Q \\equiv \\sim p \\vee \\sim q \\equiv \\text{F} \\vee \\text{T} \\equiv \\text{T}$.\nThus, whenever $P$ is True, $Q$ is also True. Hence $P \\to Q$ is always True (a tautology)."
