      "solution": "Let's test option D: $(p \\land q) \\to ((\\sim p) \\lor q)$.\nIf $p \\land q$ is True, then $p$ is True and $q$ is True.\nThen $(\\sim p) \\lor q$ is False $\\lor$ True = True.\nIf $p \\land q$ is False, the implication is vacuously True.\nThus, $(p \\land q) \\to ((\\sim p) \\lor q)$ is always True (tautology)."
